  "paper": "special-relativity",
  "argument": "arg-sr-field-derivatives",
  "title": "The x derivative, rewritten",
  "spoken": "The x derivative is gamma times the primed x derivative minus v over c squared times the primed time derivative.",
  "explanation": "The rate of change along x, written through the moving system's derivatives. Per metre on both sides.",
  "review": "draft",
  "notation": "modern-pedagogical",
  "unitSystem": "si",
  "assumptions": [
    "The moving system moves along x at speed v relative to the stationary system, with |v| < c. Modern teaching notation: gamma is the paper's beta, c its V.",
    "Partial derivatives of a field, taken in each system's own coordinates; the chain rule through the Lorentz transformation relates them."
  ],
